"""Test the momentum signal class on the collected universe.

Background: the trend-following MA-crossover class was exhaustively explored on
the collected adjusted-close universe and rejected. The short-horizon
return-reversal class (short the previous 5-day return, hold 1 day, daily
rebalanced) was exhaustively explored and rejected: every segment of every
asset showed a negative median walk-forward log return; the perturbation sweep
was flat on the null.

Momentum is the direct competing hypothesis to reversal: go LONG the previous
N-day return instead of shorting it, hold 1 day, daily rebalance. The
contraposition is clean — reversal and momentum use the same lookback window,
the same walk-forward, and the same coin-flip null; they differ only in signal
sign. If reversal loses in every segment of every asset, the momentum variant
should make the opposite mistake. This test settles whether the 5-day-lookback
direction bet is a robust edge in this universe, or whether it is noise with a
direction sign attached.

Falsification prediction: momentum either shows CONSISTENT_WITH_NOISE (no edge
anywhere) or REGIME_DEPENDENT (the positive run concentrates in one historical
regime mix, notably 2009-2013), or REGIME_STABLE_LOSS (uniformly negative —
which would be reversal winning on both sides, an inconsistency to explain).
Either outcome is a negative conclusion and closes the cell.

Method (fixed a-priori, not tuned to OOS): long the previous 5-day return;
hold 1 day; daily rebalance. Base MA(20/60) included for comparison. The two
REGIME_DEPENDENT assets from the MA run (AMZN, JPM) are run through
stress_segments over the 4 contiguous volatility blocks with both variants; the
full collected universe is swept via stress_segments_across_tickers; a synthetic
perturbation sweep (lookback 3/5/10 over the canonical regime family with a
coin-flip null) exercises the parameter-robustness gate. Determinism is
asserted via an internal independent recomputation.

Research / simulation only. No live trading or production execution.
"""
from __future__ import annotations

import json
import sys
from pathlib import Path

import numpy as np

sys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent.parent))
import research.backtest as bt
from research.data.preflight import load_manifest, sha256_file

DATASET_ID = "yf-ohlcv-universe-2009-to-2026-10-03"
SEED = 42
LOOKBACK = 5
TRAIN, TEST, WARM, OVERLAP = 252, 84, 60, 60
WINDOW = 60
N_BLOCKS = 4
MIN_SEGMENT_BARS = 400
ARTIFACT_DIR = Path.cwd() / "state" / "check_artifacts"
ARTIFACT_PATH = ARTIFACT_DIR / "momentum_results.json"


def base_signals(closes, fast, slow):
    """Past-only MA crossover (same contract as research/backtest/regime_stability)."""
    n = len(closes)
    out = [bt.Signal(date=i + 1, weight=0.0) for i in range(n)]
    fast, slow = int(fast), int(slow)
    for i in range(max(fast, slow) - 1, n):
        fm = float(np.mean(closes[i - fast + 1 : i + 1]))
        sm = float(np.mean(closes[i - slow + 1 : i + 1]))
        out[i] = bt.Signal(date=i + 1, weight=1.0 if fm > sm else -1.0)
    return out
